# Directly set the pose of one MuJoCo object.
#
# Only objects that can actually move are accepted: a `body` must be driven by a free
# joint, and for a `site` / `geom` the plugin resolves the rigid body it belongs to and
# back-computes the body pose that puts the site/geom on the requested pose (the body
# must be free as well).  Absolute writes to joint-driven bodies are rejected.
#
# `pose.header.frame_id` selects the reference frame: empty means the world frame,
# otherwise the name of a MuJoCo body the pose is expressed in.

string type
string name
geometry_msgs/PoseStamped pose

# When true the object is teleported immediately; when false the caller is expected to
# use the action variant for a smooth interpolation.
bool immediate

---
bool success
string message
